WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.200
Good morning John; it's Friday, November 7th.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.060
Almost three years ago, you and I decided
to do something that was really hard, but

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.899
that we really wanted to do.

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:11.000
Eventually, with a lot of help, Crash Course
became a thing.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.560
And a lot of teachers and a lot of students
use it.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.040
We've kept it free; it's available for anyone
with an internet connection, and it is – and

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.220
I say this with a deep love for the Pemberley
Digital stuff and SciShow and VidCon and the

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.950
Wimbly Womblys – the best thing that we
do.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.110
It is a thing that I am very proud of, and
so, with a tear in my eye, here's a look back

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.770
at the last three years of Crash Course.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.340
J: Hi, I'm John Green.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.739
This is Crash Course World History, and today
we're gonna talk about civilization.

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:37.789
H: I'm Hank Green and I wanna teach you chemistry.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:39.649
But, please, do not run away screaming.

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:43.359
H: People may not be the easiest organisms
to understand, but – you're a person, right?

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:45.059
J: Oh god, Stan, it's Me From College.

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:47.109
Me From the Past has become Me From College.

00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:48.109
This is a disaster!

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:50.300
H: Nothing escapes the long arm of ecology.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.320
H: Like any good 50 Cent song, biology is
just about sex and not dying.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.050
J: The test will last your entire life, and
it will be comprised of the millions of decisions

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.920
that, when taken together, make your life
yours.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.270
And everything – everything!

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:13.869
– will be on it.

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:28.330
[Crash Course theme music]

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.079
The only reason Crash Course works is because
people like it.

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:34.340
Most of the people who watch Crash Course
do it because they want to, not because they

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.340
have to.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.100
For the first two years of Crash Course, it
was funded by a Google grant, basically.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.539
Then that Google money ran out, and we had
to figure out how to keep making the show.

00:01:41.539 --> 00:01:42.900
So basically, we just asked.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.159
We asked people who liked Crash Course if
they'd like to give a little bit of money

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:49.640
so that it could keep existing for them, and
also for all of the other people in the world.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.640
We didn't wanna start charging for it; we
didn't wanna put it on an exclusive platform

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.481
where only people using that platform could
get it.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:58.040
We got a lot of offers to do those sorts of
things and to make fair amounts of money doing

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.040
it.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.680
We didn't want to lock the content down, but
it looked like we might have had to – BUT:

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.039
People decided to just give us money through
Subbable.

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:09.581
Crash Course relies hugely on that support
and I could never be more grateful for it.

00:02:09.581 --> 00:02:12.310
It means we get to keep making better and
more content.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.310
We've also done some partnerships; the Big
History series that we're in the middle of

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:18.300
right now is in partnership with the Bill
Gates Think Tank BGC3.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.730
And now we're working on a significantly larger
relationship with PBS Digital Studios.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.720
They're gonna allow us to basically double
the amount of content that we're doing on

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.720
Crash Course.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.950
Of course, PBS, just like Crash Course, is
largely funded by people who watch and love

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.040
PBS stuff.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.590
So it's sort of a natural fit.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.370
And we've worked with these people before;
we've liked them; we worked with them on Frankenstein

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.460
MD, and the Art Assignment.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.720
So in 2015, we're hopefully doing four Crash
Courses:

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.800
Craig Benzine, aka WheezyWaiter, will be doing
a government class.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.650
Phil Plait, who is probably the most successful
astronomy blogger in the world, will be doing

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.860
Crash Course Astronomy.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:52.290
I will be doing Crash Course Physiology –
And we're still working on it, but hopefully

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.200
we will also be doing Crash Course Economics.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.050
If you haven't checked out Crash Course yet,
there's a ton of really interesting content:

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:03.620
history, biology, and chemistry, ecology,
and literature, and soon, government and astronomy

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.980
and physiology and eCOnomics – eCOnomics?

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.960
Did I really just say eCOnomics?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.960
EcoNOMics.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:09.960
Is what I meant to say.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.370
PBS Digital Studios does a ton of really interesting
stuff as well, there's a link to their channel

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.370
in the description.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.570
And finally, unrelated to any of this, I have
an announcement to make: John and I, starting

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.500
Monday, will be doing The Twelve Days of Pizzamas.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.630
During those twelve days, John and I will
make a video every day except for the weekends.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.690
Just like Brotherhood 2.0, there's gonna be
a lot of vlogbrothers content coming at you,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:28.690
so be ready.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.790
I'm doing Monday, Wednesday, Friday next week
and then Tuesday, Thursday the week after

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.790
that.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.290
So you're gonna see a lot of Paper Towns set,
and the videos are gonna decrease in quality

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.650
cause we're gonna have to make so many of
them, and we're probably gonna go a little

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.830
bit insane, and it's gonna be great.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.210
I'm actually really looking forward to it.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.660
I feel like it's getting back to my roots,
you know?

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.650
I want a little a bit more back and forth,
I wanna feel more connected to it all, and

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.410
so this is gonna be a good two weeks.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.080
Pizzamas begins on Monday.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.000
So I'm gonna make two videos in a row, so:

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.620
John, I will see you on Tuesday, and you will
see me on Monday.

